+patch: n/a
+---
+
+# PLAN-012: Merge consecutive same-speaker segments under a duration threshold in the stored .srt
+
+## Status
+
+draft
+
+## Governing records
+
+- BDR-006: the `.srt` is the canonical transcript artifact and must stay a
+  standard, player-loadable SRT file. Merged output remains plain valid
+  SRT; no format extension is introduced.
+- ADR-007: three-file session bundle (`.md` frontmatter + `## Assist`,
+  `.srt` bilingual cues, `.wav`); cue number = segment index + 1 binds a
+  cue to the socket event index; `.srt` rewrites go through read ->
+  splice -> tmp write -> rename serialized on the writer queue. This
+  plan adds one more rewrite operation of exactly that shape.
+- ADR-005: configuration and tunables come from env vars via `zod` in
+  `server/config.ts`; the merge option is a new env var, not a UI or
+  per-session setting.
+- ADR-006 + BDR-002: no new dependencies; merge is string manipulation
+  inside existing modules.
+
+## Scope
+
+In scope:
+
+1. A new env option `TRANSCRIPT_MERGE_MAX_S` (seconds, default `10`,
+   `0` disables) parsed in `server/config.ts` and documented in
+   `.env.example`.
+2. Merge logic inside `SessionWriter`: consecutive same-speaker segments
+   fold into the previously written cue while the resulting cue span
+   stays under the threshold. Only the `.srt` on disk changes; socket
+   events, segment indices, assist `#n` tags, `active.finals`, and the
+   web display are untouched.
+3. Translation routing so a merged cue collects the translations of all
+   contributing segment indices, joined with a space in index order.
+4. Automated tests for the merge rule, the two new SRT helpers, the
+   config field, and the disabled-equals-unchanged guarantee.
+
+Out of scope: any web/display change (`groupSegments` already groups
+same-speaker finals visually); socket event or index renumbering; `.md`
+body changes (the `.md` holds no transcript lines under ADR-007, so
+"markdown and subtitle export" means the session bundle's two artifacts,
+of which only the subtitle file carries segment text); contiguous cue
+renumbering; retroactive merging of already-stored sessions; merging on
+the read path.
+
+## Contracts (literal)
+
+### Env option (`server/config.ts`, `.env.example`)
+
+```ts
+TRANSCRIPT_MERGE_MAX_S: z.coerce.number().nonnegative().default(10),
+```
+
+`.env.example` block:
+
+```
+# Merge consecutive same-speaker transcript segments into one cue when
+# the merged span stays under this many seconds. 0 disables merging.
+TRANSCRIPT_MERGE_MAX_S=10
+```
+
+`0` means disabled: with `mergeMaxS` unset or `0`, `appendSegment` and
+`appendTranslation` produce byte-identical output to today.
+
+### New helpers in `server/session/srt.ts`
+
+```ts
+// Rewrites cue `index + 1` in place: the end timestamp becomes
+// formatSrtTimestamp(endS) and ` ` + oneLine(text) is appended to the
+// first text line (the source line). A translation line already present
+// is preserved untouched. Returns the updated document, or null when the
+// cue is missing.
+export function extendCue(
+  srt: string,
+  index: number,
+  endS: number,
+  text: string,
+): string | null;
+
+// Sets the translation (last text line) of cue `index + 1`: replaces the
+// existing second text line when present, otherwise appends it. Returns
+// the updated document, or null when the cue is missing.
+export function setCueTranslation(
+  srt: string,
+  index: number,
+  text: string,
+): string | null;
+```
+
+Both reuse the `insertTranslationLine` block-scan pattern
+(`split(/\n{2,}/)`, match first line against `String(index + 1)`, verify
+` --> ` on line 2, rejoin as `` `${blocks.join('\n\n')}\n\n` ``) and the
+`oneLine` newline flattening.
+
+### `SessionWriter` surface (`server/session/writer.ts`)
+
+```ts
+export interface SessionWriterOptions {
+  mergeMaxS?: number; // seconds; > 0 enables merging
+}
+
+static async create(
+  rootDir: string,
+  meta: SessionMeta,
+  log?: WarnLog,
+  opts?: SessionWriterOptions,
+): Promise<SessionWriter>;
+```
+
+Merge rule (the only new decision):
+
+```ts
+seg.speaker === lastCue.speaker && seg.end_s - lastCue.start_s < mergeMaxS
+```
+
+- Speaker equality is on the raw `seg.speaker` label; `undefined ===
+  undefined` counts, so speaker-less runs merge too (same rule the web
+  `groupSegments` uses for display).
+- "Combined duration" is the resulting cue span `lastCue.start_s ->
+  seg.end_s`; "under" is strict `<`, so a span exactly equal to the
+  threshold does not merge.
+- No gap constraint: "consecutive" means adjacent in arrival order only.
+
+Merged cue example (threshold 10; indices 0,1 same speaker):
+
+```
+1
+00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,400
+Speaker 1: Hello. there.
+```
+
+Cue numbering keeps the `index + 1` binding for every cue that exists.
+Merged-away indices leave numbering gaps (indices 0,1,2 merged then
+index 3 -> cues `1` and `4`), which is valid SRT and keeps
+`insertTranslationLine`, `backfill`, and `cueCount` semantics exact.
+
+### Translation routing for merged cues
+
+The writer keeps three pieces of bookkeeping, all updated synchronously
+at API-call time (before the op enqueues) so behavior is deterministic:
+
+```ts
+private lastCue?: {
+  cueNo: number;
+  speaker: string | undefined;
+  start_s: number;
+  end_s: number;
+};
+private readonly cueOfIndex = new Map<number, number>(); // index -> cue number
+private readonly mergedCues = new Set<number>();         // cue numbers built by merging
+private readonly cueTranslations = new Map<number, Map<number, string>>(); // cueNo -> index -> text
+```
+
+`appendTranslation(index, text)` resolves `cueNo = cueOfIndex.get(index)
+?? index + 1` (fallback identical to today), then:
+
+- cue not in `mergedCues`: unchanged path - `insertTranslationLine(srt,
+  cueNo - 1, text)`, null -> warn + skip; on success also record
+  `cueTranslations[cueNo][index] = text`.
+- cue in `mergedCues`: record `cueTranslations[cueNo][index] = text`,
+  render `joined = entries sorted by index -> texts joined with ' '`,
+  rewrite the line via `setCueTranslation(srt, cueNo - 1, joined)`,
+  null -> warn + skip.
+
+Recording every translation (not only merged-path ones) is what lets a
+translation that landed before the merge survive the later rewrite in
+correct index order.
+
+## Steps
+
+1. `server/config.ts`: add `TRANSCRIPT_MERGE_MAX_S` to `envSchema`
+   (contract above), placed after `STT_IDLE_TIMEOUT_S`.
+2. `.env.example`: add the documented block above near
+   `STT_IDLE_TIMEOUT_S`.
+3. `server/session/srt.ts`: add `extendCue` and `setCueTranslation` per
+   the literal contracts.
+4. `server/session/writer.ts`:
+   - `SessionWriterOptions`, optional 4th `create` param, stored
+     `mergeMaxS` (default `0`).
+   - New private bookkeeping fields above.
+   - `appendSegment(index, seg)`: when `mergeMaxS > 0` and the merge
+     rule holds against `lastCue`, set `cueOfIndex`, add to
+     `mergedCues`, update `lastCue.end_s`, and enqueue the same
+     read -> `extendCue` -> tmp write -> rename cycle
+     `appendTranslation` uses; null -> warn + skip (defensive; the cue
+     was just written). Otherwise append `formatCue` exactly as today
+     and reset `lastCue`/`cueOfIndex` for the new cue.
+   - `appendTranslation(index, text)`: the two-path routing above;
+     non-merged path code unchanged.
+   - `create`, `appendAssist`, `renameSpeakers`, `finalize`, queue:
+     unchanged.
+5. `server/session/manager.ts`: pass
+   `{ mergeMaxS: this.config.TRANSCRIPT_MERGE_MAX_S }` as the fourth arg
+   to the single `SessionWriter.create` call in `start` (~line 186).
+   Nothing else changes: `handleFinal` still assigns an index,
+   broadcasts, translates, and assists every final.
+6. `server/app.test.ts`: add `TRANSCRIPT_MERGE_MAX_S: '0'` to the
+   `parseConfig` env in `beforeEach` so the existing e2e suite keeps
+   exercising the disabled path (two same-speaker finals exist in the
+   assist suite and would merge under the default `10`). Add one e2e
+   test that builds a second app instance with
+   `TRANSCRIPT_MERGE_MAX_S: '5'`, emits two same-speaker finals, and
+   asserts a single merged cue in `stored.srt`.
+7. Tests per the Test plan section.
+8. Commit, then log via `CONTEXTS/04-logs/event.py`.
+
+## Test plan
+
+- `server/session/srt.test.ts`:
+  - `extendCue`: updates the end timestamp and appends ` ` + text to the
+    source line; preserves an already-present translation line; returns
+    null for a missing cue; flattens embedded newlines.
+  - `setCueTranslation`: appends a second text line when the cue has
+    only a source line; replaces an existing translation line; returns
+    null for a missing cue.
+- `server/session/writer.test.ts` (new `describe` for merging):
+  - merge under threshold: `Speaker 1` segs idx0 `0->2 'Hello.'`, idx1
+    `2->3.4 'there.'` -> single cue `1` with
+    `00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,400` and `Speaker 1: Hello. there.`;
+    a third same-speaker seg extends the same cue again (chain merge).
+  - no merge across different speakers: idx1 `Speaker 2` -> separate
+    cue `3` (numbering gap is the documented contract).
+  - no merge over threshold: same speaker, `seg.end_s - lastCue.start_s
+    >= mergeMaxS` -> separate cue.
+  - disabled = unchanged: writer created with no opts (and once with
+    `mergeMaxS: 0`) -> two same-speaker short segs produce exactly the
+    current two-cue output.
+  - translations into a merged cue: `appendTranslation(0, 't0')` +
+    `appendTranslation(1, 't1')` on a merged cue render `t0 t1` on the
+    cue's second line; also the order where t0 lands before the merge
+    and t1 after.
+  - numbering: `cueCount`/file shows gaps but `index + 1` binding holds
+    for cues that exist.
+- `server/config.test.ts`: default `10`; `'0'` parses to `0`; a negative
+  or non-numeric value is rejected.
+- `server/app.test.ts`: `TRANSCRIPT_MERGE_MAX_S: '0'` in the shared
+  env (see step 6) plus one enabled-path e2e asserting the merged cue.
+- Manual: one short live session with merge on; open the `.srt` in a
+  player next to the `.wav` and confirm merged cues play and
+  translations sit on the second line.
+
+## Risks and notes
+
+- Assumption: "markdown and subtitle export" means the session bundle's
+  `.md` + `.srt`; under ADR-007 only the `.srt` carries transcript text,
+  so it is the only file whose content changes. The `.md` (frontmatter +
+  `## Assist`) stays byte-compatible.
+- Assumption: the feature is on by default at `10`s; `0` is the disable
+  switch. If the reviewer prefers opt-in semantics, the field becomes
+  optional with no default - a one-line schema change, noted here so the
+  plan does not need re-drafting.
+- Assumption: "combined duration" = resulting cue span and "under" = `<`.
+  Boundary (`span == threshold`) does not merge.
+- Assumption: speaker-less segments merge with each other
+  (`undefined === undefined`), matching `groupSegments`. If "same
+  speaker" should require a defined label, the rule gains a
+  `seg.speaker !== undefined` clause - also a one-line change.
+- Cue numbering gaps after a merge are deliberate (preserves `index +
+  1` binding); SRT players ignore numbering. Consequence: assist `#n`
+  tags and socket `index` values may reference merged-away indices with
+  no matching cue - cosmetic, consistent with ADR-007's index semantics.
+- Transient state: between a merge rewrite and the absorbed segment's
+  translation landing, the cue shows merged source with the pre-merge
+  translation; the merged-cue translation path then rewrites the line to
+  all pieces joined by ` ` in index order. Out-of-order translation
+  arrivals still render correctly because the render is map-driven, not
+  append-driven.
+- Speaker renames still do not rewrite already-written cue prefixes;
+  merging inherits that existing caveat.
+- `insertTranslationLine` keeps its current contract (null on an
+  already-translated cue) for non-merged cues; only merged cues take the
+  new set/replace path.
+
+## Definition of Done
+
+- [ ] `npm run typecheck` clean; `npm test` green.
+- [ ] Automated tests cover: merge under threshold, no merge across
+      different speakers, no merge over threshold, disabled =
+      byte-identical output.
+- [ ] `TRANSCRIPT_MERGE_MAX_S` parsed with default `10`, `0` disables,
+      documented in `.env.example`.
+- [ ] With merging enabled, a session `.srt` stores merged cues (joined
+      source text, extended end time, joined translation line) while
+      socket events and the `.md` are unchanged.
+- [ ] Plan status updated and completion event logged via `event.py`.
-- 
