+## 21:47 - Implement PLAN-012: merge short same-speaker .srt segments
+
+**Scope:** server/session, server/config | **Type:** Feature | **Commit:** 74496f2 @ doc-centric
+
+## Scope
+server/session, server/config
+
+## Type
+Feature
+
+## Commit
+- **Hash:** 74496f2
+- **Repo:** doc-centric
+- **Message:** Merge short same-speaker transcript segments in the stored .srt (PLAN-012)
+- **Author:** Satoshi Man <mrvuong.bitcoin@gmail.com>
+- **Date:** 2026-11-05 21:47:48 +0700
+
+## User request
+Implement the newest PLAN in CONTEXTS/03-implement-plan/ exactly per its scope and DoD. Commit, tick DoD items, set status: implemented, and log via CONTEXTS/04-logs/event.py.
+
+## Reason
+PLAN-012 (review_count 1, patch applied, developer instruction to implement). Merging is on by default at 10s with 0 as the disable switch; span comparison is strict <; speaker equality is on the raw label so speaker-less runs merge like groupSegments. Translation join is map-driven so out-of-order arrivals render in index order.
+
+## Description
+Added TRANSCRIPT_MERGE_MAX_S (default 10, 0 disables) parsed via zod in config.ts and documented in .env.example. SessionWriter gained mergeMaxS plus lastCue/cueOfIndex/mergedCues/cueTranslations bookkeeping: consecutive same-speaker segments fold into the previous cue via extendCue while the span stays under the threshold, leaving numbering gaps that preserve the index+1 cue binding. appendTranslation routes merged-away indices to the surviving cue and rewrites the last text line with all contributing translations joined in index order (setCueTranslation); non-merged cues keep the skip-if-translated contract. New srt.ts helpers extendCue and setCueTranslation follow the insertTranslationLine block-scan pattern. manager.ts passes the config value into SessionWriter.create. Tests: srt helper unit tests, writer merge describe (threshold, speaker switch, speaker-less, chain, disabled-identical, translation ordering, numbering), config parsing tests, and an app e2e with a second instance at mergeMaxS=5 asserting one merged cue with joined translation. Existing e2e suite pinned to TRANSCRIPT_MERGE_MAX_S=0.
+
+## Files changed
+.env.example
+CONTEXTS/03-implement-plan/PLAN-012-merge-short-segments.md
+server/app.test.ts
+server/config.test.ts
+server/config.ts
+server/session/manager.ts
+server/session/srt.test.ts
+server/session/srt.ts
+server/session/writer.test.ts
+server/session/writer.ts
+
+## Notes
+Merged-cue translation rewrite deviates from ADR-007's skip-if-translated rule scoped to merged cues only, as recorded in the plan. meta.segments counts stored cues so merged sessions show fewer segments than emitted finals (documented cosmetic consequence). Manual live-session player check not performed; automated coverage substitutes.
